WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
- Who you gonna call?

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.260
Not them, 9-1-1.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.302
Let's talk about it.

00:00:04.302 --> 00:00:05.898
(beeping sound)

00:00:05.898 --> 00:00:07.250
- [Dispatcher] 911, what's your emergency?

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.470
- [Caller 1] I think I hear
a baby crying, in the wall.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.860
- [Dispatcher] How's the baby on the wall?

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.050
- [Caller 1] No, no, no, not
on the wall, in the wall.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.190
There's a baby inside my wall.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.465
I think someone flushed
a baby down the toilet.

00:00:18.465 --> 00:00:19.800
- What?

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.350
- [Voiceover] 12 seconds later.

00:00:22.377 --> 00:00:24.250
(Mike laughing)

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.770
- I thought that's just a joke
we did as medical students,

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.980
listening to the wall
to hear the other room

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:29.990
with the stethoscope.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.070
Oh my God.
(knocking on wall)

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.925
(knocking on wall)

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:35.580
(baby crying)

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.830
A premature baby that cries loudly enough

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.290
that you can hear it through a wall

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.310
and a pipe and it's
surviving through water,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.337
I mean, like, this is just ridiculous.

00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:46.054
(wall crunching)

00:00:46.054 --> 00:00:47.071
(tool grinding)

00:00:47.071 --> 00:00:49.737
- [Fireman 1] All right, it's off.

00:00:49.737 --> 00:00:51.229
Get the head out, Bobby, get the head out.

00:00:51.229 --> 00:00:52.540
- You've got to push from below.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.190
- This is not how I've delivered babies,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.535
when I delivered babies, not from pipes.

00:00:56.535 --> 00:00:59.345
(suspenseful sound)

00:00:59.345 --> 00:01:00.219
(Mike laughing)

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:01.819
There's so much wrong with this.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.278
- [Fireman 1] Okay, pull
her out, pull her out.

00:01:04.278 --> 00:01:05.640
Pull her out.
- The fakest baby, too.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.517
- [Paramedic] All right, she's
not breathing, starting CPR.

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:09.416
Come on.

00:01:09.416 --> 00:01:10.249
- Correct form with the hands,

00:01:10.249 --> 00:01:12.480
but gotta push a little deeper, man.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.220
This is such a ridiculous scene

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.770
that I would say this would never happen,

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:18.150
but I know one of you is
going to pull out an article

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.670
where one person in some small rural area

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.340
this happened to, and they survived,

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.220
and you guys are gonna be like "See, Mike,

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.859
you don't know what you're
talking about as a doctor."

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:26.692
(dramatic music)

00:01:26.692 --> 00:01:28.322
- [Father] Marika, Marika,
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:28.322 --> 00:01:30.060
- Your daughter just had a baby.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.620
We have to get her to the hospital.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.090
- No, is that the mother? No, screw her!

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.400
- She's bleeding out,
- Look what she did!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.233
- She's a child!

00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:36.320
- That's ridiculous.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.370
You don't get to play judge and jury.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.930
You gotta save everyone's life.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.530
Especially, when it comes to a child

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.750
who's lost a lot of blood.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.590
Who knows if she's in
her right state of mind?

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.790
- Yo, if this baby dies, it's on you.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.280
- Why would the baby die?

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.410
And why is it on her?

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.269
What does she have to do with anything?

00:01:51.269 --> 00:01:52.326
- [Dispatcher] Who is choking you?

00:01:52.326 --> 00:01:54.230
Do you know him?

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.290
- Oh, that's a boa.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.540
Snake fans, help me out here.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.373
That's a problem.

00:01:58.373 --> 00:01:59.640
Um, yes, call for help.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.490
- Bobby, it's no use.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:01.780
That thing is like 10 feet long,

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.190
its constriction strength is
like 50 pounds per square inch.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.290
- Everyone is Dr. House.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.101
- [Bobby] Crap, it's getting really tight.

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:10.400
Think we're gonna have to put it down.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.606
- Okay, stand back.

00:02:11.606 --> 00:02:14.106
(playful music)

00:02:14.106 --> 00:02:15.090
- Spartacus.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.500
- Yeah, well, it was him or you and,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.290
faced with a situation like that,

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.697
I always choose to save
the more attractive one.

00:02:22.697 --> 00:02:24.890
(Mike sputters)

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.810
- I hope he gets fired
after a statement like that.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.373
- [Sam] Would you ever speak
to a patient like that?

00:02:28.373 --> 00:02:31.160
- I would not, respectfully.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.346
- [Dispatcher] What's your emergency?

00:02:32.346 --> 00:02:33.711
- [Caller] Shark! Shark!

00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:35.020
A man's been attacked by a shark!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.859
- Oh man!

00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:36.692
- [Dispatcher] What
beach are you on, ma'am?

00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:37.525
- [Caller] We're not on a beach,

00:02:37.525 --> 00:02:38.510
we're on the freeway.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.356
- What?

00:02:39.356 --> 00:02:41.260
(man screaming)

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.387
This show is so incredible.

00:02:44.237 --> 00:02:45.070
(man screaming)

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:45.903
- [Paramedic] What the hell?

00:02:45.903 --> 00:02:46.840
- Tiger shark.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.070
We were transporting her
for release into the wild,

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:49.960
truck jackknifed.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.150
- The truck jackknifed
then how did the guy's arm

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.800
end up inside the shark?

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.460
Someone needs to explain that to me.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.837
- Can you wait that long or just-

00:02:56.837 --> 00:02:59.759
- No, no, don't kill
her, she's come so far.

00:02:59.759 --> 00:03:00.592
(Mike chuckles)

00:03:00.592 --> 00:03:02.910
- Award for empathy
goes to that gentleman.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.377
He's getting his arm literally
torn off and he's like,

00:03:06.377 --> 00:03:07.964
"Think about the shark."

00:03:07.964 --> 00:03:11.358
(tool grinding)
(man grunts)

00:03:11.358 --> 00:03:13.766
(bones crunching)

00:03:13.766 --> 00:03:16.960
(suspenseful music)

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.010
- Alright, let's get him transported now.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:20.683
- [Paramedic 2] Nice and easy.

00:03:20.683 --> 00:03:21.770
- [Paramedic 3] Put some
pressure on that brachial artery.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.070
- From a brachial artery laceration,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.210
you can die in seconds.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.910
- How deep his arm is.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.100
- Yeah, his full arm.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.250
- It's the whole thing is inside.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.483
- And behold, the salabhasana.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.010
- Everything hurts.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.050
The baby, is he okay?

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.410
- I'll check your baby right now, okay.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.330
I'm going to touch you
right here in your stomach.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.870
Okay, there's no trauma to the abdomen.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.570
- Why would there be
trauma to the abdomen?

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.800
She's doing yoga.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.451
- Easy, I'm gonna take you..

00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:47.558
(Woman groans)

00:03:47.558 --> 00:03:48.740
- All right, I'm going
to take care of that.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.573
You take care of this.
- Yeah, go, go.

00:03:49.573 --> 00:03:50.406
- Here we go, I got you, I got you.

00:03:50.406 --> 00:03:52.350
- I think I'm having contractions.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.100
- Are they real contractions though?

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.933
- What's your name?

00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:55.766
- Beth.

00:03:55.766 --> 00:03:57.160
- Okay, I need a cup of water for Beth.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.190
- Am I in labor?

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.555
- I think it's Braxton Hicks.

00:03:59.555 --> 00:04:00.800
(Mike sputtering)

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.620
- I mean, Braxton Hicks contractions

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.820
are something reasonable to think about,

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.650
how he knew that instantly
without understanding

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.130
if she's totally in labor
or not, I have no idea,

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:11.321
that's kind of ridiculous.

00:04:11.321 --> 00:04:13.390
- We're gonna get you nice and
relaxed and hydrated, okay.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.950
- There's just like really good questions

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.426
to be asked here, not are you thirsty?

00:04:17.426 --> 00:04:18.720
(water splashing)

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.742
- Oh my God, my water broke!

00:04:20.742 --> 00:04:21.923
(Mike laughing)

00:04:21.923 --> 00:04:23.330
- What is this class?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.740
- 911, what's your emergency?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.573
- My son.

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:27.030
He hit his head on the diving board,

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.863
and he's not breathing.

00:04:27.863 --> 00:04:29.540
Oh my God, he's turning blue.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.270
- I need you to perform CPR on him.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.030
- Interesting that they'd say
to perform CPR right away.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.700
I would like to check for a pulse first,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.720
but if he's turning
blue, that probably means

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.760
he's not breathing.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.790
He's pulseless.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.900
He's nonresponsive.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.490
Again, chest compressions,
chest compressions,

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.340
chest compressions.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.000
It's not about mouth to mouth anymore.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.730
It's about pumping the heart

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.410
and causing it to push the
blood throughout your system,

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.579
which still has some oxygen in it.

00:04:51.579 --> 00:04:52.987
- [Paramedic] Come around,
starting compressions.

00:04:52.987 --> 00:04:54.900
- I mean, I would have loved to see them

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:55.980
check for a pulse here.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:56.970
- [Paramedic] Was he underwater?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.330
- [Mother] I don't know
a few minutes, maybe.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.500
- Those are terrible chest compressions.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.930
They have to be at least two inches deep.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.870
You have to brisk breaking ribs

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.980
in order for them to be effective.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.670
Remember the job of the chest compressions

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.450
is to actually compress the heart.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.140
And if you're just doing
them superficially,

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.604
you're just doing it for a show.

00:05:11.604 --> 00:05:13.300
(record scratching)

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.040
They are doing it for a show.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:15.873
I guess that's okay.

00:05:15.873 --> 00:05:17.473
- As soon as help arrives,

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.853
most people just hang up.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.530
- Yeah.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:24.520
What are you sad?

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.283
- Ah, okay, just hang on.

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:30.002
(nail gun shooting)
(both gasping)

00:05:30.002 --> 00:05:31.750
(Mike chuckles)

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:32.690
- That's a no-no.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.230
Never point anything
with "Gun" at yourself.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.063
Nail gun,

00:05:37.063 --> 00:05:38.060
paintball gun,

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:38.957
cap gun.

00:05:41.044 --> 00:05:41.877
- [Sam] Gun?

00:05:41.877 --> 00:05:42.710
- Gun.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:43.543
- [Woman] Dad?
(Sam laughing)

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:46.370
(suspenseful music)

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.450
- He needs a level one
trauma surgeon stat.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.518
- I don't know what I'm supposed to do.

00:05:49.518 --> 00:05:50.580
- Do I pull it out?
- Don't pull it out.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.710
- No, do not remove the nail.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:53.910
Help is on the way.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:54.880
- I'm gonna clear your shirt,

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.370
so we can see what we're working with.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.190
- Dude, do not clear anything.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.830
Put him on the stretcher

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.270
and bring him to the hospital

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.220
where emergency surgery can happen.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.470
- You hit the bull's-eye.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.627
- Who makes jokes like that?

00:06:07.627 --> 00:06:08.730
"Hit the bullseye."

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.750
- [Paramedic 1] Nice and easy.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:10.730
Bring it around.
- [Paramedic 2] Sir?

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:11.563
- [Paramedic 1] Careful.

00:06:11.563 --> 00:06:13.630
- If he hit a lung, he's also
gonna have a collapsed lung

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.463
there as well.

00:06:14.463 --> 00:06:15.705
- [Paramedic 1] Take a
few deep breaths for me.

00:06:15.705 --> 00:06:16.820
(Mike laughing)

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.240
- Bro, just put him on the stretcher.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.810
Bring him to the hospital, stop!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.330
Stop torturing the man.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.300
- I need to get you to the
hospital for pericardiocentesis

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.680
that's where they'll drain the fluid.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.520
- Dude, you don't even know what

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.040
is the extent of the damage.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.150
This is ridiculous that
they're diagnosing him

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.200
already knowing everything
that's happening.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.640
Do you know why I'm getting so angry?

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.510
Because too often patients come in

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.000
and someone does this like

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.160
incorrect diagnosis thing on the go.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.010
And then I have to come in

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.800
and correct all this misinformation

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.090
and it confuses patients.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.030
It's hard enough to hear
what's happening here,

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.297
when you have a nail gun in your heart,

00:06:47.297 --> 00:06:48.750
but then imagine trying to deal with

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.440
who's right, who's wrong.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.590
- Of course I did, why?

00:06:52.593 --> 00:06:53.426
(machine beeping)

00:06:53.426 --> 00:06:54.787
- That is not a good rhythm.

00:06:54.787 --> 00:06:59.180
(suspenseful music)
(paramedic breathing heavily)

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.370
Yep, that's a problem, that is a problem.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.830
- They'll fix it at the hospital,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.130
but only if he's not dead.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.850
- In this case, there
is nothing you can do.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.070
The only thing you can do
is try and resuscitate,

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.630
but like pulling the nail out,
pushing the nail further in,

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:14.880
you're only going to do more damage.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.110
- Come on, you're not
leaving your daughter

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.053
hanging like that.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.381
- We got a pulse.

00:07:19.381 --> 00:07:20.214
- Oh!

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:24.670
Yep, heart's beating again.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.670
- Yeah heart's beating again,

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.960
but he's actively bleeding out.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.010
There's like zero use
for celebrating here.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.180
It's quite often that a patient
gets resuscitated with CPR,

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.040
only to lose their pulse
shortly thereafter.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.860
So like, this is not a win by any means.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.220
- I can't move my neck.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.053
- Oh no.

00:07:39.064 --> 00:07:40.434
(ambulance wailing)

00:07:40.434 --> 00:07:43.550
Is that, is that a Phineas
Gage situation right now?

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.330
- He's got a piece of
rebar through his skull.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.680
How is that even possible?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:47.680
- It's possible.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.240
Brain tissue has no nociceptors,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.160
it can't feel pain.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.590
- That is actually true.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:55.850
However, the meninges feel
pain, skin feels pain,

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.690
and you know, all those
videos circulating around

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:58.950
with the person playing an instrument,

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.260
while they're doing brain surgery.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:03.397
That can happen because the
brain has no pain receptors.

00:08:03.397 --> 00:08:05.170
- Well, why aren't you guys
cutting me out of here?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.580
- It's complicated.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.413
- Why?

00:08:07.413 --> 00:08:08.360
- You've been injured Jim.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.568
- Well how bad is it?

00:08:09.568 --> 00:08:11.203
- It's not good.

00:08:11.203 --> 00:08:13.820
- What is this conversation
thing that happens?

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:16.140
This is not real, just do your job.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.430
You're 911.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.730
Don't start taking selfies

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.729
and face timing your friends.

00:08:20.729 --> 00:08:21.562
- [Dispatcher] 911 What's your emergency.

00:08:21.562 --> 00:08:23.800
- I'm at Metro Fitness on Hollywood.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.109
My boss is burning up.

00:08:25.109 --> 00:08:26.120
- [Dispatcher] Do you mean he's feverish?

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.610
- [Caller] No, that's not what I mean.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.453
- [Caller] I um, I
smelled something burning.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.507
- Oh my God!

00:08:34.507 --> 00:08:36.830
(fire burning)

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.280
- We all kept trying to
tell him to get it fixed.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.820
She couldn't have unplugged it?

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.320
- Why the hell didn't he just get out.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.320
- Might've had a stroke.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.770
- How did he know he has a stroke.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.570
I mean these guys with
their like House MD,

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.200
ridiculous diagnoses.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.200
- He too may have had a stroke,

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.750
drugs could be an underlying
cause, what was he on?

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.740
- What is this guy?

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.640
He's on drugs.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.473
How do you know?

00:09:01.473 --> 00:09:02.306
Look at him.

00:09:02.306 --> 00:09:04.350
What do you mean, look at him?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.550
- Starting compressions.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.943
- Good compressions.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.130
Yeah, that's normal, so keep going.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.630
I mean, not normal, but normal

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.700
if your skins so damage,

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.540
but the chest compressions override that.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.130
'Cause remember when
someone's heart stops,

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:19.963
that means they're dead.

00:09:19.963 --> 00:09:21.670
So whether or not you damage their skin,

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:22.503
they're already dead.

00:09:22.503 --> 00:09:23.510
Try and bring them back.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.343
- Nope, he's gone.

00:09:24.343 --> 00:09:26.260
- What do you mean, nope he's gone?

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.670
Do more chest compressions!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.860
Try and bring him back!

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.110
My hands got dirty.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:30.943
He's gone.

00:09:30.943 --> 00:09:32.320
I'm getting mad at the show.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:35.540
- [Man 1] We have a stunt, so daring.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.570
- [Man 2] A video, so bold.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.403
- [Man 1] It might-

00:09:38.403 --> 00:09:39.342
- [Man 2] Just-

00:09:39.342 --> 00:09:40.410
- [Both] Break the internet!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.930
- Oh my god, is this a YouTube challenge?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.994
A TikTok challenge?

00:09:43.994 --> 00:09:44.827
- Spin.

00:09:44.827 --> 00:09:47.827
(upbeat rock music)

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:52.530
- What is the purpose of this?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.903
How is the bike not moving?

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.500
How long has that poor guy been on there?

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:58.600
He's probably like

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.433
completely out of it.

00:09:59.433 --> 00:10:01.260
- Hey, can you hear me?

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.093
Oh!

00:10:02.093 --> 00:10:03.760
- Oh, that's a problem.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.750
Need an ophthalmology consult stat.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:06.670
- Could be G-LOC.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:08.710
- G-force poisoning
from the force of spin?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.610
- Right now, all his blood
is pooling inside his head.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.630
It's pressing against his brain,
which is why he's out cold.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.670
- I don't know if that's G-LOC.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.250
G-LOC is when you essentially have

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.540
your blood go to the
lower part of your body

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.960
and you're not getting enough circulation.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.980
And This is a very big
problem for F-16 pilots,

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.760
I actually flew a 16, so I studied this.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.575
Click the video down below.

00:10:28.575 --> 00:10:30.658
- [Paramedic] Here we go.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.900
I would not do this without
an ophthalmologist on site.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.870
I would not do this.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:37.140
Like there's no way firefighters

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:38.840
or first responders would do this.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.810
Wow, that was...

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:44.010
Super.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.870
- Eventually could you die
from spinning that much?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.640
- I mean, you could die
from anything for like,

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.850
can you run to your death?

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:50.850
Yeah.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.320
Speaking of G-forces
check out this video of me

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.720
flying an F-16.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.220
That's right, I experienced 9.2 Gs.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.053
Check it out.

00:10:58.053 --> 00:10:59.500
As always stay happy and healthy.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.410
But really check this out,

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.427
I was like (imitates plane noises).

00:11:02.783 --> 00:11:05.616
(soft beat music)

